A||||8||Raydar||Fiero deficit in the Northwest?||||1||
Z||000000||Raydar||07-01-2001||10:35 PM||||Okay, just got back from spending 10 days exploring the mountains in Washington and Oregon, and the Oregon coast. Lots of GREAT twisty roads, and beautiful scenery. (Unfortunately, I was in a rental. A Dodge Intrepid, of all things. What a tank!)<BR>I saw Mt. St. Helens, Mt. Rainier, Crater Lake, and more lighthouses than I can name. <BR>And I only saw six Fieros, the whole time. Saw a red 85 (I think) coupe in a car lot. Don't remember the city.<BR>Saw a gold 86 coupe and a silver 88 (or 87) coupe in Astoria. <BR>Saw a black 85 GT (or maybe an 86-87 SE) in Depoe Bay.<BR>Saw a silver 85 (I think) in Gold Hill.<BR>Saw a <I>flawless</I> blue 87 coupe in Grant's Pass. <P>The West coast is beautiful. If you've never been there, I highly recommend it. <BR>If you know what a homebody I am, you understand what a ringing endorsement this is.<P>And take your Fiero! You'll be glad you did.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 07-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Darekin||07-02-2001||04:11 PM||||I Actually live in Washington, and its beautiful here. I own a fiero up here, and in Redmond I have seen 3... Two silvers and a black. I guess there is actually a Euro Fiero here, the steel body bigger engine model. I wish there were more fieros here, teach more of these rice boys a lesson... I can't hold them all myself... This friday I should be breaking the 200hp barrier with my mods... so I should be able to hold off a few... let me know the next time yer up.<P>------------------<BR>Darekin<BR>============<BR>1985 Fiero GT<BR>Performance Exhaust<BR>Hypertech Chip<BR>K&N Filter<BR>Accel Dist. coil.<BR>Hi-Flo Cat. Inst 7/6<BR>Cold Air Intake 7/6||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||07-02-2001||07:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Darekin:<BR><B>I guess there is actually a Euro Fiero here, the steel body bigger engine model. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmmm... <BR>Never seen one of those.<BR>Musta got fupped duck and missed it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Sad to say, I probably won't be back there any time soon. My wife went out to Beaverton (Portland 'burb) to work on a project, and we decided to make a vacation out of it.<P>Good luck with the project. 200 HP from a 2.8 is some serious "stones".<P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"||||reg||1
Z||000003||sjp777||07-02-2001||09:08 PM||||Yes, there seems to be a distinct lack of Fieros up here.<P>What's even worse is there never seems to be any shows within less than a 12 hour drive to SF.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>On the up side, since there are so few, the ones that are here get a lot of looks.<P>The drive from Portland to the coast on the WA side of the Columbia River is what Fieros were made for. Twisty roads, few cops or traffic and unbelievable scenery.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg"> <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||onfire||07-03-2001||03:24 AM||||Actually there are quite a few Fiero's up here. They are still in hibernation. But the weather is getting nicer, so the Fiero's will come out. I usually see 1 or 2 a week. Different ones too, not the same ones.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/onfiresig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||AusFiero||07-03-2001||04:13 AM||||hmmmm I know of 8 Fieros within 160 miles of my place. That make em scarce here?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>One is my Red 86.5 t-topped GT. Next closest in order are:<BR>Red 85 GT - Poorly customised, poor shape in general except the paint.<BR>Yellow 84/85? 2M4 coupe - Average condition stock daily driver.<BR>Black 86 coupe 4cyl - Run down but a registered driver.<BR>Black 87 GT - Good condition all round. Not a show car but a really neat daily driver.<P>Red 87 GT - Average daily driver.<P>Red 88 GT - Immaculant low mileage car, rarely driven and with the Fiero number plates I tried to get. Well still could if I pay a grand for them, which isn't likely.<P>Know of others but I wouldnt consider them close. <P>My next Fiero has been held for me, not  a close one, just gotta get the bucks together. Is an 88 GT t-topped car, RHD, partially converted to a 3.8 ltr, not running. But good value in Australia at AU$6000 or about US$2800.  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||07-03-2001||11:36 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>...an 88 GT t-topped car, RHD, partially converted to a 3.8 ltr, not running. But good value in Australia at AU$6000 or about US$2800.  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's the exchange rate?!<BR>That makes a Commodore SS nearly reasonable, instead of outrageously, obscenely expensive!! <BR>Bet it would cost a fortune to ship one here, though.<P>Never dreamed there were that many Fieros around you.<BR>Good luck with that 88! <P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||07-03-2001||11:44 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by onfire:<BR><B>...They are still in hibernation. But the weather is getting nicer, so the Fiero's will come out. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That makes sense. I guess summer happens way later in the NW. Thought the ocean breeze would moderate it a bit. WRONG! I nearly froze my a$$ off. And we went up on Johnson's Ridge (Mt. St. Helens) in the rain.<BR>I have never_been_so_cold in my life.<BR>(For contrast, it's 87 degrees at 11:30 AM in Atlanta.)<P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 07-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Darekin||07-03-2001||04:53 PM||||In the higher elevations it is colder... but at sea level not too bad. its 78 degrees out right now... thats not bad. <P>------------------<BR>Darekin<BR>============<BR>1985 Fiero GT<BR>Performance Exhaust<BR>Hypertech Chip<BR>K&N Filter<BR>Accel Dist. coil.<BR>Hi-Flo Cat. Inst 7/6<BR>Cold Air Intake 7/6||||reg||1
